u need to employ a  full-time manager to buy a house or to  build a portfolio they get paid on  results everybody within your property  business you know whereas if you're  running an actual business then you need  to employ people if you're buying  properties you buy a house you pay a  solicitor to complete on the legal side  of things you don't pay the solicitor  unless he does the job you pay him on  results then once you've done that and  you've paid your mortgage broker and  your solicitor you pay a management  company it's also clock for property I  think is the number one definitely the  number one way to get passive income and  that's why I love property so much I got  some friends they're millionaires  they're doing really well but they're  constantly you know dealing with staff  and problems I've got staff I have  problems  but property yeah I think I think it  wins it wins all right  next which city is better for rent  income Manchester or Birmingham that's  from Marius which rents are probably  higher in Birmingham but it doesn't  matter about where rents are higher it  matters where you're going to get a  better return on investment in London  the rents are really high but the houses  are also really high so it's all about  the return on investment which where  would you get that return on investment  probably similar  I mean maybe Manchester I similar it  also depends the so many factors you  can't just say what's better Manchester  or Birmingham I'd the person who asked  me that question so Marius I would say  which city do you have better contacts  with which city do you know that ins and  outs of the good streets and the bad  streets you know it's you can make any  city work as long as you know the city  as long as you've got good connections  personally I don't have properties in  Manchester but I have many in Birmingham  but that's because I know Burma better  so don't look at the rent  always look at the return on investment  all right last one t